# Ignore list for the RUNNER image only. BuildKit prefers
# <dockerfile-path>.dockerignore over the root .dockerignore, which exists for
# the server image and excludes the TypeScript workspaces — the very things
# this image is made of.
#
# Same red line as everywhere else (docs/DATA-AND-LEGAL.md): nothing under
# data/ enters an image.
.git
data
node_modules
deps
dashboard/dist
dashboard/dist-public
dashboard/node_modules
collector/node_modules
runner/node_modules
sdk/node_modules
wiki/node_modules
minimap/node_modules
module
.env

# Everything .gitignore keeps out of git stays out of the image. build-images.sh
# builds from a git archive of the commit, and the branch-image workflow from a
# clean checkout, so none of this exists there; these lines are for a hand-run
# `docker build` from a working checkout. Dockerignore patterns are anchored at
# the context root where .gitignore's match at any depth, hence the `**/`.
**/data
**/node_modules
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/.claude
**/.wrangler
infra/fleet.json
dashboard/public/og.png
**/*.log
**/.DS_Store
